  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DSU-ONJL Youth Council Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Our pilot project aims to empower Colombian youth councillors by addressing the challenges they face in gaining influence within local governance. Through focused training in leadership, advocacy, and political engagement, we provide the tools they need to drive change. The project has two components: 1) DSU and ONJL will conduct a five-day course in Bogot&#xfffd; for selected youth council leaders, drawing on DSU&#xfffd;s extensive experience in political training. This course addresses key issues, such as limited advocacy skills. 2) Using a trainers-by-trainers model, participants will lead local sessions to share their knowledge with peers. This approach aims to reach and educate over 450 Colombian youth councillors.</narrative>
  </description>
